    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Charles returns three months after his first visit. He has stayed well while touring. He keeps one naloxone spray at home and one in his travel bag, and the people he travels with have been shown how to use it. He has had no opioid or other drug use and no cravings, including on long tours and in hotel rooms, which he names as the times he is most careful. His eyes have been comfortable. He has had no falls; in hotels he is shown around each new room on arrival and keeps his belongings in fixed places. He has started working on a plan for any future pain with Dr. Fenwick. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Recovery</td><td>No use and no cravings; aware of travel as a time to be careful</td></tr><tr><td>Naloxone</td><td>At home and in his travel bag; travel staff shown how to use it</td></tr><tr><td>Eyes</td><td>Comfortable</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>None; spoken orientation to each new hotel room</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

